  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Catalog",
    "overview": "Wave sets the owner's library the way a record label sets its catalog (the ECM cover program is the touchstone): artwork sits in wide, calm, tinted fields and the type around it is small and exact. Calm here comes from alignment, not from emptiness. Every margin, row, tile and the A–Z spine snaps to one 8dp cell, so a screen of tens of thousands of tracks still reads as ordered furniture rather than density.\n\nThe ground is tinted, never plain white or black: fog blue-grey in light, night slate in dark, and every neutral is a step on one tonal ramp drawn from that ground. Hierarchy is quiet. The large title is light, not bold; lists use one type size and rank by weight and tint; labels are small tracked capitals, like the catalog line printed under a sleeve. Two chromatic voices only: a deep teal for what is active, an ember for what is loved or playing.\n\nThe world rejects the category default it was chosen against: bold large titles, chevron-and-icon rows, rounded \"card\" chrome around artwork, and a single accent on pure black or white. Components are fully custom (chosen over Material 3), but Android's own conventions still hold: system and predictive Back work, touch targets are 48dp, and the theme follows the system light/dark setting.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Tinted fog / night-slate ground; neutrals from one ramp (OKLCH hue ~215).",
      "One 8dp cell module for every dimension.",
      "Artwork as photographs: square, unrounded, unframed.",
